---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import {SITE} from "@data/site";
---
<Base title="Contact the Foundation — VirtEngine" description="Contact DETIO FOUNDATION LTD about VirtEngine, collaboration, open-source development, or licensing.">
<div class="container-site"><div class="content-hero"><p class="kicker">CONTACT / DETIO FOUNDATION LTD</p><h1>Start a useful conversation.</h1><p class="intro">Questions about the project, a technical contribution, or a possible collaboration? Here is how to reach the people behind VirtEngine.</p></div>
<div class="contact-grid"><section class="contact-card"><p class="kicker">GENERAL &amp; FOUNDATION ENQUIRIES</p><h2>Talk to the Foundation</h2><p>For project questions, research collaboration, accessibility feedback, or licensing enquiries, email the project contact. Include what you are trying to do and the relevant page or document.</p><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email} ↗</a><p class="local-note">Opens your email app. You review and send the message yourself.</p></section><section class="contact-card"><p class="kicker">CODE &amp; DOCUMENTATION</p><h2>Contribute in the open</h2><p>Explore the repository before reporting a bug or proposing a change. For a reproducible issue, include the version, expected behaviour, and steps to reproduce. Public issues are visible to others.</p><a class="text-link" href={SITE.github}>Explore the VirtEngine repository ↗</a><p class="local-note">Do not post personal identity documents, credentials, or private keys in public issues.</p></section></div>
<div class="editorial-grid" style="margin-top:40px"><div class="reading"><h2>Before you get in touch</h2><p>For a first look at the technology, start with <a href="/learn/how-the-marketplace-works">how the marketplace works</a>. Infrastructure operators can review the <a href="/providers">provider requirements</a>. The <a href="/network">network status page</a> explains planned launch stages and their conditions.</p><p>VirtEngine is in development. This contact page does not book computing capacity, enrol a provider, verify identity, or confirm a commercial service. It gives you a direct route to discuss the project.</p></div><aside class="info-card"><h2>Organisation details</h2><dl><div><dt>LEGAL ENTITY</dt><dd>DETIO FOUNDATION LTD</dd></div><div><dt>AUSTRALIAN COMPANY NUMBER</dt><dd>699 651 771</dd></div><div><dt>STRUCTURE</dt><dd>Not-for-profit public company limited by guarantee</dd></div><div><dt>PROJECT</dt><dd>VirtEngine open-source protocol</dd></div></dl><a class="button primary" href="/about">Read about our mission →</a></aside></div></div>
</Base>